{"name":"Scent layering (body wash, lotion, fragrance)","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":24,"casual":{"lead":["Scent layering uses products from the same scent family, such as body wash, lotion and fragrance, so the smell builds, lasts longer and feels coherent.","The fragrance industry promotes a version of it: scented bath oil, shower gel or lotion in the morning, a lighter eau de toilette in the afternoon, and perfume at pulse points in the evening. General references say hydrated skin holds fragrance longer. No published trials of layering were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People pick matching or complementary products, apply wash and lotion after showering, then add fragrance on top, and refresh through the day."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Fragrance ingredients can be allergenic, and more scented products means more potential exposure. No layering-specific studies were found."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Staphylococcus Aureus Swabbing and Decolonization Before Neuromodulation Procedures: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36198512/","source":"Neuromodulation : journal of the International Neuromodulation Society","year":2023,"cites":null,"kind":"Meta-Analysis"},{"title":"Pre-surgical Nasal Decolonization of Staphylococcus aureus: A Health Technology Assessment.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36160757/","source":"Ontario health technology assessment series","year":2022,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Role of pH in skin cleansing.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34137035/","source":"International journal of cosmetic science","year":2021,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Randomized Controlled Trial of Preoperative Topical Decolonization to Reduce Surgical Site Infection for Staphylococcus aureus Nasal Swab-Negative Mohs Micrographic Surgery Patients.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30204741/","source":"Der